# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Suyeon Ju et al. (2025). Application of pretrained universal machine-learning interatomic potential for physicochemical simulation of liquid electrolytes in Li-ion batteries.
#   Digital Discovery. doi:10.1039/d5dd00025d  arXiv:2501.05211v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2501.05211v1 (sha256 c6c8ccecd7aa57ea...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 131 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: an application of the pretrained SevenNet-0 model (with
# a D3 dispersion correction added) to carbonate solvents and Li-salt
# electrolytes, and one fine-tuned model (SevenNet-FT) trained on 150
# structures to correct liquid densities. Encoded: the molecular energy
# check of the pretrained model and the fine-tuning run with its
# retention-test errors.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
